#!/usr/bin/env python3
# =============================================================================
# h96-waydroid - opt-in Android-in-a-container installer for the H96 Max V58
#                (RK3588 / Mali-G610, KDE Plasma on X11).
#
# Waydroid runs a full Android (LineageOS) system in an LXC container sharing the
# host kernel. Two things this box needed before Android would even boot are now
# baked into the v4.3 kernel: CONFIG_ANDROID_BINDER_IPC/BINDERFS (builtin) AND
# CONFIG_PSI=y (Android 11+ lmkd/init hard-require /proc/pressure - without it the
# container boots then dies in ~15s). `status` verifies both.
#
#   h96-waydroid                     interactive menu / status
#   h96-waydroid status              binder / PSI / session / image / GPU report
#   h96-waydroid install             apt repo + waydroid + weston + cgroup/nft fixes
#   h96-waydroid init gpu [dir]      Panthor HARDWARE image (Mali-G610), fixed-size window
#   h96-waydroid init gapps|vanilla  latest official LineageOS (downloaded once, then stashed)
#   h96-waydroid init custom <dir>   use your OWN system.img + vendor.img pair
#   h96-waydroid size [WxH]          set the launch window / render size (picker if no arg)
#   h96-waydroid state save|list|load|delete   save/restore Android state across image switches
#   h96-waydroid spoof [dev|off]     report a common phone (Aurora Store / Play compatibility)
#   h96-waydroid start               launch the UI in a nested Weston window (X11)
#   h96-waydroid stop                stop session + container + weston
#   h96-waydroid hw [on|off]         re-apply / remove the Panfrost GPU wiring + verify
#   h96-waydroid remove              full uninstall (keeps nothing)
#
# IMAGE PROFILES.
#   * gpu       - a Panthor-in-image Android 11 build (LineageOS 18.1, the Rockchip
#                 RK3588 board image) with Mesa/Panfrost compiled IN. This is the ONLY
#                 way to drive the Mali-G610 in hardware here. `init gpu` overrides the
#                 image's tiny 960x512 to your chosen size so Android FILLS the window.
#                 Requires the image files - see `init gpu` below; they are not bundled
#                 (~5 GB, kept in gpu-images).
#   * gapps /   - the latest official Waydroid LineageOS image (Android 13). RECOMMENDED.
#     vanilla     It DOES drive the Mali-G610 in hardware: measured on this board,
#                 `GLES: Mesa, Mali-G610 MC4 (Panfrost), OpenGL ES 3.1 Mesa 26.0.1`, GPU load
#                 reaching 50 percent at 1000 MHz under UI activity. Newer Mesa than the
#                 Panthor image, a current Android, and a signed upstream build. About 900 MB.
#   * custom    - an image you supply yourself. It MUST be an arm64 Waydroid-style
#                 system.img + vendor.img PAIR (LineageOS-for-Waydroid or similar); a ROM
#                 zip, OTA payload or plain GSI will not boot. GPU accel only if that image
#                 has Mesa/Panfrost compiled in - `hw on` verifies and reports honestly.
#
# IMAGES ARE NEVER RE-DOWNLOADED. Every image (downloaded or supplied) is stashed under
# /etc/waydroid-extra/{gpu,los,custom}-images and symlinked into the auto-detect path, so
# switching profiles is instant and offline. `init vanilla fresh` forces a new download.
# The stashes are ~2-5 GB each and are NOT part of the released system image.
#
# WHY THE WINDOW IS FIXED-SIZE. Any window-manager geometry change - drag-resize, edge
# snap / quick tile, maximise, fullscreen - makes Weston reconfigure its X11 output. The
# Waydroid client renders Android at ONE fixed size and cannot follow that reconfigure: it
# drops off the compositor ("libwayland: error in client communication") and the window
# goes PERMANENTLY black. KWin ignores a min-size-only hint when quick-tiling, so the
# launcher pins WM_NORMAL_HINTS min == max and the window simply is not resizable. Pick the
# size instead with `h96-waydroid size` (it warns if you exceed the display resolution).
#
# THE X11 WRINKLE. This box runs KDE Plasma on X11 on purpose (Wayland breaks the
# GPU/mpv path on this BSP). Waydroid's show-full-ui wants a Wayland compositor,
# so `start` runs a nested Weston window inside the X session and points Waydroid
# at it - the standard KDE-on-X11 approach. Nothing about the desktop changes.
#
# Auto-elevates via sudo for install/init/hw/stop/remove. `start` runs as the
# desktop user (it needs your X DISPLAY). Bring your own APKs; no app is bundled.
# =============================================================================
import os, sys, shutil, subprocess, pwd, time, glob

BANNER_LIB   = "/usr/local/lib/h96/banner.sh"
LAUNCHER     = "/usr/local/bin/h96-waydroid-launch"
LOCKWIN      = "/usr/local/bin/h96-waydroid-lockwin"  # pins the window to a fixed size
DESKTOP      = "/usr/share/applications/h96-waydroid.desktop"
WESTON_SOCK  = "h96-waydroid"                         # deterministic Wayland socket
